---
// The web viewer's page (docs/adr/0008) in the site's theme: the viewer (loaded by src/components/Footer.astro), which
// draws the next Mech's GLBs beside this page at viewer/ (web/build.py PUBLIC, docs/adr/0019, #649) in the Preset the
// header's Theme bar picks or the viewer's own mix (#806, #819) and moves this switch into its bar: a button per Stage
// (macros.py stage_switch, from model/geometry.py STAGES, #720); Cansin's build's line on its stand-in Skin (stand_in).
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import { published, stand_in } from '../macros.json';

const { buttons } = published.stages;
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Viewer', tableOfContents: false }}>
  <p>
    The next Mech as its model has it so far, Stage by Stage: its bare Skeleton, realistic and anatomical, until the
    Theme bar at the top picks a Preset, or any Shape in any Palette from the selects under it: Stage 1 the eye block
    on its test stand, Stage 2 adds the Torso, the neck and the boards, Stage 3 the jaw; Skin shape none shows Stage 3 bare, its Skeleton alone. Drag to turn it,
    scroll or pinch to zoom, play each gesture and take it apart.
  </p>
  <Fragment set:html={stand_in} />
  <div class="noggin-viewer" data-stage={buttons.at(-1).glb} data-zoom>
    <nav aria-label="Stage">
      <span>Stage</span>
      {buttons.map((b) => <button data-stage={b.glb}>{b.label}</button>)}
    </nav>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>

<style is:global>
  .noggin-viewer canvas { height: 60vh; } /* the bar under it in view on a laptop */
</style>
